From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:52:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8781-zinwa-q25: describe the GNSS
 receiver

The Q25's L1 LNA enable is GPIO25, as in the stock DT's gps_l1_lna
states; function 2 gives the pin to the GNSS DSP. The stock DT also
carries L5 states on GPIO87, but the stock engine has no L5 DSP image for
MT6789, so they are left out.

The receiver sits under the CONNSYS node with a default state that holds
the pin low as a GPIO and an active state the driver selects while
/dev/gnssN is open.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts    | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
index f2c361bd..293595bb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
@@ -1311,3 +1311,28 @@
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
  * Physical QWERTY: RP2040 on I2C6, see &i2c6 above.
  * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
+
+/* GNSS L1 LNA enable on GPIO25; function 2 hands the pin to the GNSS DSP. */
+&pio {
+	gnss_lna_off_pins: gnss-lna-off-pins {
+		pins {
+			pinmux = <Q25_PINMUX(25, 0)>;
+			output-low;
+		};
+	};
+
+	gnss_lna_dsp_pins: gnss-lna-dsp-pins {
+		pins {
+			pinmux = <Q25_PINMUX(25, 2)>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&consys {
+	gnss {
+		compatible = "mediatek,mt6789-gnss";
+		pinctrl-names = "default", "active";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&gnss_lna_off_pins>;
+		pinctrl-1 = <&gnss_lna_dsp_pins>;
+	};
+};
